<ArticleLayout slug="youtube-shorts-specs" ctaLabel="Create your account" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">The YouTube Shorts size rule fits in one line: any square or vertical video of three minutes or less, uploaded at up to 1080p. Every platform value below comes from YouTube's own help pages, Google's ad help and, for the comparison, each network's own documentation.</p>

  <p>Reviewed October 8, 2026.</p>

  <h2>What size is a YouTube Short?</h2>

  <p>Shoot and export vertical 9:16 at 1080p, which is 1080 by 1920 pixels. YouTube accepts any square or vertical video up to three minutes as a Short and says the maximum upload resolution for Shorts is 1080p. In hubStudio, Shorts autopilot writes each clip at exactly that size, and the YouTube module marks it Short.</p>

  <p>The frame is the easy part. Teams get caught on what sits around it: the thumbnail, a music claim on a clip that runs past a minute, and the ad that only plays its first 60 seconds.</p>

