  <h2>FAQ</h2>

  <h3>What size should a YouTube Short be?</h3>

  <p>Vertical 9:16 at 1080p, which works out to 1080 by 1920 pixels. YouTube's help center says Shorts upload at a maximum resolution of 1080p and that any square or vertical video up to three minutes counts as a Short. The pixel pair is arithmetic on that 1080p figure, not a number YouTube prints.</p>

  <h3>How long can a YouTube Short be?</h3>

  <p>Up to three minutes, for videos uploaded on or after October 15, 2024. Videos uploaded before that date stay long-form even if they would qualify today. One catch: YouTube's English help page says a Short over one minute with an active Content ID claim is blocked worldwide; the French page says new ones under three minutes are no longer blocked automatically from September 24, 2026. Clear the audio either way.</p>

  <h3>Does a YouTube Short have to be 9:16?</h3>

  <p>No. YouTube's rule is a square or vertical aspect ratio, so 1:1 qualifies as well as 9:16. Vertical fills the phone screen, which is why most teams export 9:16. A horizontal 16:9 video is never classified as a Short, however short it is, and a horizontal Shorts ad is served with blurred bars above and below.</p>

  <h3>Can I upload a YouTube Short in 4K?</h3>

  <p>YouTube's help pages say you can upload Short videos at a maximum resolution of 1080p. Export at 1080 by 1920 and you're working at the ceiling YouTube states. The custom Shorts thumbnail is a separate file and can be larger: YouTube asks for 2160 by 3840 pixels at 9:16, at least 640 pixels tall.</p>

  <h3>Can I upload YouTube Shorts from a computer?</h3>

  <p>Yes. In YouTube Studio, click Create, then Upload videos, and pick a square or vertical file of three minutes or less. You can select up to 15 at a time, then complete each draft's details before publishing. On a phone, the YouTube app's Shorts camera records clips that add up to three minutes, or uploads a vertical video.</p>

  <h3>How do I change a YouTube Shorts thumbnail?</h3>

  <p>Pick a frame from the Short, before or after upload, and add text or filters. For a custom image, use YouTube Studio on a computer with a verified account: Content, then Shorts, then the Short, then Upload file under Thumbnail. Make it 9:16. A 16:9 thumbnail on a vertical video is swapped for an automatic 4:5 crop on some pages.</p>

  <h3>How long can a YouTube Shorts ad be?</h3>

  <p>Up to three minutes, but only the first 60 seconds play in the Shorts feed, so Google's ad help recommends ads under 60 seconds. Use 9:16. The ads run in Demand Gen, Video view, Video reach, Performance Max, App and Reservation campaigns, between organic Shorts, and the viewer can swipe past at once.</p>

  <h3>Why is my YouTube Short over a minute blocked?</h3>

  <p>YouTube's English help page says any Short over one minute with an active Content ID claim, manual claims included, is blocked globally: it can't be played, recommended or monetized. The French version says new Shorts under three minutes are no longer blocked automatically from September 24, 2026. If yours is blocked, remove the claimed audio, cut it under 60 seconds or resolve the claim. Blocked or not, a claim can cost the Short its monetization.</p>
